CBS subsidiary WWL reported that an assistant in Tangipahoa indicated 200 flooded houses.
Residents were evacuated into two churches, both of which have now been flooded.
Robby Miller's leader said authorities had rescued 72 people and seven pets washed up by the floodwaters.
