"Once the water starts to go back, they'll be able to go back into their homes," he said.
In the town of Hammond the municipality of Tangipahoa, nearly two dozen streets have been closed due to the floodwaters and sandbags have been allocated to residents who hope to be able to keep the water out of their homes and shops.
