“There were concerns that... state institutions had knowingly ignoring such behavior because of “politically correct” hypersensitivities regarding ethnicity and religion.”
Sir Eric made 50 recommendations to clean up the system, including prohibiting political activists from editing postal ballot documents to stop "electoral harvests."
The report, considered by Theresa May, also calls for tougher registration reviews to prevent the electoral register from being used for immigration and welfare fraud purposes.
Considering options to ask voters for your ID pre-election.
Use unremovable ink on a person's finger as soon as they cast their vote to prevent someone from voting twice.
Carrying out systematic checks on a person's nationality to ensure they are eligible to vote.
A three-year limit to applications for an automatic postal vote.
Prohibition that political activists process complete postal votes and envelopes of postal votes.
Give the police the authority to set up barriers around polling stations.
A change in the law that facilitates an intimidation charge under the Representation of the People's Act 1983 (People's Representation Act 1983).
photography ban in polling stations.
Requirement that only English may be used in polling stations (except Wales).
Intensifying training to ensure employees enforce the rule that voters go into the voting booth alone.
Sir Eric falls over Metropolitan Police and finds it "amazing" that no criminal charges have been filed after Tower Hamlet's case.
"The electoral court has declared Lutfur Rahman and his deputy unsuitable due to a litany of corrupt and illicit practices," he said.
He became pleased guilty due to a number of reasons - according to the high requirements in the criminal proceedings.
He also criticises the ineffective "chopping-off controls" of town halls' electoral registration departments.
Sir Eric said: "Last year's court ruling in Tower Hamlets was a warning signal.
Our country bears a proud heritage as the mother of parliaments, but the worrying and covert spread of electoral fraud and denial of some authorities threatens this good reputation.
