Barcelona are the record winners in this competition with eleven successes so far.
Ma Long in his own league to table tennis gold
Rio de Janeiro - The Chinese Ma Long is the new table tennis Olympic champion.
The 27-year-old defeated his compatriot and "defending champion" Zhang Jike 4:0 (12,5.4.4) in a one-sided finale on Thursday in Rio de Janeiro.
With this, the world ranking first won the "Golden Grand Slam" with successes at the World Cup, World Cup, World Tour final tournament and Olympia.
Bronze went to Japan's Jun Mizutani.
As expected, the two Chinese made it into the final game and made the title among themselves.
So it was clear that for the third time in a row, a Chinese woman would win the single title in the sign of the Five Rings.
Former SVS-NÖ legionnaire Ryu Seung-min from South Korea was the last non-Chinese on the top Olympic podium.
Ma and Zhang were left alone at the record, between the sets and time-outs they had no coaches with them.
They had retreated to the stands and let their protégés loose on each other alone in fair competition.
“I’ve played the matches so far for my country.”
"I'm playing for myself in the final," Zhang had consequently said.
After the game, gold and silver medalists posed with the China flag.
The match itself was unexpectedly one-sided.
Ma really struggled with his 28-year-old opponent only in the first set.
After that, he determined the pace at the plate and only left Zhang a total of 13 points.
Due to Ma's superiority, the expected rousing match didn't develop.
However, there were plenty of breathtaking ball changes to be seen.
Mizutani won the match for bronze against 40-year-old Vladimir Samsonov 4:1.
The Belarusian had contracted a rib injury in his quarter-final against German European champion Dimitrij Ovtcharov, was then undergoing medical treatment, "ultimately" with sheet metal.
By the way, the Swedes Jan-Ove Waldner (38/2004) and Jörgen Persson (42/2008) had finished fourth in a similarly high tannisk.
