Conducting is a necessity for him.
You see it in each of its movements, in his gaze, it's his life!
It's such a huge chance to share this musical experience with him.
We both have a rather southern temperament, a fire, a passion and also a cheerful approach to life, that's very important at all!
For American director Philip Wm. McKinley, "West Side Storry" is highly up-to-date: "This play is about prejudice and fanaticism."
