Jewish director smashes Berlin hotel because Israeli primary election has been removed after "Arabic" call - RT News
A French director with Jewish roots unleashed a media turmoil after revealing that the Kempinski Bristol Hotel in Berlin did not list an Israeli arreal as Arab guests "required," according to an employee.
Claude Lanzmann, author of the Holocaust documentary "Shoah," skipped his anger at the Kempinski Bristol Hotel in Berlin by writing an open letter to the German newspaper FAZ.
